cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Pricing Transparency and Subscription Friction in Consumer AI
  Products: A Cross-Sectional Documentation Audit of 76 Products
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or the instruments, please cite it. And
  please read limitations-register.md first — it lists what the
  numbers cannot support.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Kaya
    given-names: Mucahit
    affiliation: AI Tools Police
repository-code: 'https://github.com/'
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-08-17'
keywords:
  - pricing transparency
  - documentation audit
  - consumer AI
  - subscription pricing
  - pre-registered
  - open data
abstract: >-
  A cross-sectional documentation audit of 76 consumer AI products
  across 15 categories, coded against a pre-registered 37-variable
  instrument from official vendor documents only. No product was
  used, trialled, purchased or operated. The central finding is a
  contrast rather than a level: these vendors disclose what a buyer
  needs in order to sign up, and not what a buyer needs in order to
  budget. 57 of the 64 products with a metered generation step do
  not document whether the buyer is charged when a generation fails.
  The release carries the full audit trail, including 78 dated
  deviations and a note documenting 33 ways a documents-only audit
  of live web pages goes wrong.
